<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1610">1610</a>–<a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as James Butler, 12th Earl of Ormond, James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormond, 1st Duke of Ormond</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde, was an Irish nobleman who led the royalist side in Ireland in the wars of the 1640s and went into exile after Cromwell's conquest. He served as Lord Lieutenant of Ireland under both Charles I and Charles II, and was made a duke in 1661 after the Restoration. He was among the most powerful men in Ireland of his century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-duke-of-ormonde.jpg" alt="James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Lely_(1618-1680)_(style_of)_-_James_Butler_(1611%E2%80%931688),_1st_Duke_of_Ormonde,_in_Garter_Robes_-_1171123_-_National_Trust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
